ITEMS=[]
def Q(stem,key,d1,d2,d3,why):ITEMS.append((stem,[key,d1,d2,d3],why))
Q("Under the Act, which authority has the statutory power to issue firearm licences once the applicable requirements are met?",
 "The Registrar","The Designated Firearms Officer","The Minister of Police","The Appeal Board",
 "Section 6 gives the power to issue licences to the Registrar. Applications usually pass through the local Designated Firearms Officer, but the DFO does not issue them.")
Q("A resident must deliver a competency application to the official responsible for the area where the resident ordinarily lives. Which official is identified in section 9?",
 "The Designated Firearms Officer","The station commander of the nearest station","The Registrar at national level","The accredited training provider",
 "The application is delivered to the Designated Firearms Officer for the area where the applicant ordinarily resides, not straight to the Registrar or to a trainer.")
Q("An applicant challenges a refused competency application under section 133. Which body may confirm, vary or reverse the decision?",
 "The Appeal Board","The High Court on review","The Minister of Police","The Designated Firearms Officer",
 "Section 133 gives the Appeal Board the power to confirm, vary or reverse the challenged decision.")
Q("A person is convicted of an offence listed in section 103. Which body makes the judicial determination about the person's fitness at that stage?",
 "The trial court","The Registrar after an inquiry","The Appeal Board","The Designated Firearms Officer",
 "Section 103 concerns the determination by the court that convicts the person. It is separate from the Registrar's own section 102 inquiry.")
Q("A person has completed the required knowledge and practical training and seeks SAPS recognition that they can handle firearms safely and know the law. Which document is being sought, before any firearm licence?",
 "A competency certificate","A section 21 temporary authorisation","A permit to possess ammunition","A training provider's accreditation",
 "A competency certificate records that the person is competent. It is a separate step and does not replace a licence for an ordinary firearm.")
Q("A competent applicant wants continuing authority to possess a specific ordinary firearm for an approved purpose. Which document directly concerns that particular firearm?",
 "A licence issued for that firearm","A competency certificate for that type of firearm","A section 21 temporary authorisation","A permit to possess ammunition for it",
 "Section 11 requires a separate licence for each firearm, although several licences may appear on one document. Competency alone does not authorise possession.")
Q("A sports-shooting organisation seeks official recognition under section 8 so that it can play its statutory role for members. What status is it applying for?",
 "Accreditation","A dealer's licence","A business firearm licence for its range","A competency certificate in its own name",
 "Accreditation concerns whether the organisation is suitable and able to carry out its statutory functions.")
Q("The Registrar permits possession under section 21 for a specified period and subject to stated conditions. What kind of permission is this?",
 "A temporary authorisation","A licence for occasional sport-shooting","A permit to possess ammunition","A written storage authorisation",
 "Section 21 provides temporary authorisation, with its period and conditions set by the Registrar.")
Q("A first-time competency applicant has no approved exception and is only 19 on the day the DFO receives the application. Which section 9 requirement is not met?",
 "The minimum age of 21","The citizenship or residence requirement","The fit and proper requirement","The knowledge training requirement",
 "The ordinary minimum age is 21 on the date the DFO receives the application. The Registrar may allow an under 21 application only for compelling reasons.")
Q("A first-time applicant holds only a temporary work visa. Which section 9 requirement for an ordinary competency certificate is at issue?",
 "Citizenship or permanent residence","The minimum age requirement","Proof of employment in South Africa","A sponsor's declaration from an employer",
 "Section 9(2)(b) requires South African citizenship or a permanent South African residence permit. A temporary visa is neither.")
Q("An applicant meets the age and residence conditions but has a record showing a tendency toward assault. Which requirement does this call into question?",
 "Being fit and proper","The minimum age requirement","Freedom from substance dependence","Having a fixed residential address",
 "Competency requires being fit and proper, of stable mental condition and not inclined to violence. Meeting the age and residence rules is not enough.")
Q("An applicant is addicted to a prescription painkiller, even though the application form is otherwise complete. Which specific section 9 condition is implicated?",
 "Not being dependent on such a substance","Being of stable mental condition","The minimum age requirement","Completion of the practical training",
 "Section 9 requires that the applicant not be dependent on any substance with an intoxicating or narcotic effect. Stable mental condition is a separate listed requirement.")
Q("A first-time applicant has passed practical handling but has not completed the prescribed assessment on the Firearms Control Act. What training evidence is still missing?",
 "Proof of the legal knowledge assessment","A repeat of the practical assessment","A medical fitness certificate","A declaration from a hunting association",
 "Section 9 separately requires successful completion of the prescribed test on knowledge of the Act and the practical training. One does not replace the other.")
Q("A learner has passed the assessment on the Act but has not done the prescribed hands-on safe-handling course and test. What evidence is missing?",
 "Proof of the prescribed practical training","A second assessment on the Act","A letter from a dedicated association","A safe inspection report from the DFO",
 "Knowledge of the Act does not replace the prescribed practical training and assessment that section 9 requires.")
Q("An ordinary individual application includes the completed form and required supporting information but omits the biometric material required by section 6. What is missing?",
 "A full set of fingerprints","A certified copy of the identity document","Proof of a compliant safe","A motivation letter for the firearm",
 "Section 6 requires the prescribed application to include a full set of the applicant's fingerprints. The other items are not biometric material.")
Q("An individual applies for an ordinary firearm licence but has never been assessed and found competent by SAPS for that type of firearm. Under section 6, which prerequisite is absent?",
 "A competency certificate","An accreditation certificate","A section 21 temporary authorisation","A written storage authorisation",
 "Subject to the Act's specific provisions, section 6 prohibits issuing a licence to a person who does not hold the relevant competency certificate.")
Q("A private individual applies in their own name, not on behalf of a company or trust. Which legal description fits the applicant?",
 "A natural person","A juristic person","A nominated responsible person","An accredited association",
 "A natural person is an individual human being, as distinct from a company, trust or other juristic entity.")
Q("A company wants a licence in connection with its lawful business and must nominate an individual to apply for it. What kind of applicant is the company?",
 "A juristic person","A natural person","An accredited association","A licensed dealer",
 "Section 7 deals with applications by juristic persons, which must act through a nominated natural person.")
Q("A company's licence names the individual who acts for the company under section 7. What statutory role does that individual hold?",
 "The responsible person","An additional licence holder","The company's accredited representative","A security officer in its service",
 "The nominated individual is the responsible person and is treated as the holder of the licence for the purposes of the Act.")
Q("An organisation recognised by the Registrar under section 8 issues the membership declaration a dedicated applicant needs. What is its legal status?",
 "An accredited association","A licensed dealer","A juristic licence holder under section 7","A registered training provider",
 "The declaration must come from the appropriate accredited association, not from just any club or business.")
Q("A business firearm licence states the purpose for which the company may use the firearm. Which instrument contains that restriction?",
 "A condition stated on the licence","The licence application form","A regulation under the Act","A notice published in the Gazette",
 "Section 20 requires the licence to specify its business purpose, and use is limited to that purpose. The restriction is on the licence itself.")
Q("A generally applicable rule sets requirements for prescribed safe custody under powers granted by the Act. What type of subordinate rule is this?",
 "A regulation","A licence condition","A firearm-free zone notice","A court order",
 "The Act allows regulations to prescribe details such as safe-custody requirements. A licence condition applies only to one licence.")
Q("After the required consultation, the Minister formally makes certain premises a firearm-free zone under section 140. Which publication gives that designation its statutory form?",
 "A notice in the Gazette","A sign displayed at the premises","A regulation made by the Registrar","A letter to the owner of the premises",
 "Section 140 provides for a notice in the Gazette declaring premises or categories of premises firearm-free zones. Signs may follow, but the notice is what gives it legal effect.")
Q("A person supplies a residential address and declares the information in the prescribed form. What is this information part of?",
 "The application","The licence conditions","The firearm register","A storage authorisation",
 "It is information supplied in the application. Knowingly giving false or misleading application information is an offence.")
Q("Before a section 102 unfitness decision, a person must be allowed to explain why the declaration should not be made. Which procedural protection is directly involved?",
 "A chance to give reasons against it","A trial before a criminal court","An automatic stay of the decision","A prior review by the Appeal Board",
 "Section 102 requires the Registrar to give the person a reasonable opportunity to advance reasons before deciding.")
Q("A person appearing in a section 102 inquiry wants a lawyer to assist and speak on their behalf. Which entitlement applies?",
 "They may be legally represented","Only a family member may assist","Lawyers are excluded from the inquiry","A lawyer may attend but not speak",
 "Section 102 expressly permits the person to be represented by a legal representative.")
Q("A person who made a statement is called to a section 102 inquiry. The affected person wants to question that witness through a lawyer. What does the Act allow?",
 "They or their lawyer may examine the witness","Only the Registrar may question the witness","The witness statement must be accepted unchallenged","Their lawyer may attend but not question anyone",
 "The affected person may examine a witness who is called, or have their legal representative do so.")
Q("The Registrar receives the affected person's explanation and supporting material in a section 102 inquiry. What must the Registrar do before deciding?",
 "Duly consider the matter and the relevant facts","Treat the original notice as the final decision","Refer the matter to a criminal court","Let the DFO decide on the Registrar's behalf",
 "The Registrar must duly consider the matter and the relevant facts. The notice of the inquiry is not itself the decision.")
Q("Sworn information states that a person told a neighbour he would stab her. Which section 102 ground is directly raised?",
 "A stated intention to injure someone","Leaving firearms unsecured","Supplying misleading application information","Being dependent on alcohol or drugs",
 "An expressed intention to kill or injure oneself or another with a firearm or dangerous weapon can support the statutory inquiry.")
Q("Evidence shows that an owner repeatedly leaves firearms lying in an unlocked bedroom drawer. Which section 102 ground is directly raised?",
 "Not taking prescribed safekeeping steps","A threat to injure someone with a weapon","A final protection order against them","Giving false information to the Registrar",
 "Failure to take the prescribed steps for safekeeping is an express ground for considering unfitness.")
Q("An owner knowingly lied on a form submitted under the Act. Which section 102 ground does the dishonesty raise?",
 "Supplying false or misleading information","Neglecting to store the firearm safely","Expressing an intention to harm someone","Being subject to a final protection order",
 "Providing false or misleading information required under the Act is a ground for the Registrar's unfitness process.")
Q("A magistrate grants a final order against a firearm owner after his partner applied to the court because of abuse at home. Which section 102 ground is directly raised?",
 "A final protection order against him","A threat involving a dangerous weapon","Misleading information in an application","Failure to report a lost licence card",
 "A final protection order under the Domestic Violence Act is an express ground for the Registrar to consider unfitness through the required procedure.")
Q("The Registrar considers a new licence request and decides not to grant it. Which type of administrative decision has occurred?",
 "Refusal of the application","Cancellation of a licence","A declaration of unfitness","Suspension pending appeal",
 "Refusal concerns an application that has not been granted. Cancellation applies to a licence that already exists.")
Q("After the required notice and consideration of representations, the Registrar ends an existing licence because its conditions were breached. Which decision is described?",
 "Cancellation under section 28","Refusal of an application","Lapse of the licence","A declaration of unfitness",
 "Section 28 allows cancellation of an existing licence on the stated grounds after the required process. A lapse happens by operation of law, not by decision.")
Q("An organisation no longer meets the criteria for its section 8 recognition. After the statutory process, that recognition is withdrawn. Which decision is described?",
 "Cancellation of its accreditation","Refusal of a licence application","Cancellation of its members' licences","A declaration of unfitness against it",
 "This is cancellation of accreditation. It does not by itself cancel members' individual licences.")
Q("After the section 102 procedure, the Registrar finds that a person may not possess firearms. Which decision causes the broader section 104 consequences?",
 "A declaration of unfitness","Cancellation of one licence under section 28","Refusal of a renewal","Withdrawal of a temporary authorisation",
 "A declaration of unfitness affects all competency certificates, licences, permits and authorisations under section 104, not just one licence.")
Q("An owner lodges a complete licence-renewal application within the statutory period, but the Registrar has not decided it by the original expiry date. What does section 24 provide?",
 "It stays valid until the Registrar decides","It expires on its original expiry date","It stays valid for 30 more days only","It stays valid for 90 more days only",
 "Section 24(4) provides that if a renewal application is lodged within the period in section 24(1), at least 90 days before expiry, the licence remains valid until the application is decided.")
Q("A person holds a section 12 additional licence because they live on the primary licence holder's premises, then moves elsewhere. What is the statutory consequence?",
 "The additional licence lapses and must be returned","The additional licence moves with the holder","The additional licence stays valid until renewal","The additional licence becomes a primary licence",
 "The additional licence lapses when its holder moves from the premises and must be returned forthwith.")
Q("A person declared unfit under section 102 appeals the decision. While the appeal is pending and no decision has set it aside, what is the position?",
 "The unfitness remains in effect until it is finalised","The unfitness is suspended until the appeal is heard","Lodging the appeal restores the licences temporarily","One firearm may be kept during the appeal",
 "Section 104 states that the unfitness remains in effect pending finalisation of the appeal.")
Q("A person relies on a section 21 authorisation whose document specifies a limited period. What determines how long that temporary permission lasts?",
 "The period the Registrar sets","Ten years, like a section 15 licence","Five years, like a section 13 licence","Until the holder applies for a licence",
 "The Registrar determines the period of a section 21 authorisation. It does not take the term of any ordinary licence.")
assert len(ITEMS)==40
